WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.973
A number on a form is only useful if you can trust it.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.812
Is it from the right box?

00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:10.063
Did a digit slip?

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:13.300
And who has time to check every one by hand?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.625
Every number, traced to its page.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.856
On the page, each document wears a badge for the form it holds: W-2,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.968
1098 or 1099.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.790
Reading them is one command each.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.784
Here the W-2 and the mortgage statement are read.

00:00:30.784 --> 00:00:33.782
Every box is found by the words of its label,

00:00:33.782 --> 00:00:36.714
so a payroll company's own layout reads too,

00:00:36.714 --> 00:00:40.045
and each reading says how many of its checks pass.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.248
Each value is saved with its page, its place on it,

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:48.851
and the exact text it was read from.

00:00:48.851 --> 00:00:53.117
A check throws out any value whose text isn't on that page,

00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:58.685
and the form's own arithmetic is checked: box 4 must be 6.2 percent of box 3.
